cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReasonedOps in research, teaching, demos, or derived work, please cite this software."
title: "ReasonedOps"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cheng"
    given-names: "Gigi"
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: 2026-08-21
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
url: "https://github.com/gigichengnc/reasoned-ops"
abstract: >-
  ReasonedOps is a retrospective rebuild of an HKMU Hackathon 2026 concierge concept
  into a reproducible evidence-aware service-operations research/software prototype.
  It is organised around Operate, Audit, and Evaluate: unstructured service requests
  become explainable routing recommendations; machine and human decision history is
  preserved separately from observed outcomes; and downstream evaluation first checks
  whether a comparison and method are supportable before reporting adjusted evidence.
  Regression/ANCOVA is one method inside the Evaluate layer rather than the product
  identity. Current quantitative evidence is synthetic or hand-authored development
  evidence and does not establish real-world service improvement, causal effects,
  private-data pilot approval, or production readiness.
keywords:
  - "service operations"
  - "human-in-the-loop"
  - "evidence-aware evaluation"
  - "ANCOVA"
  - "regression"
  - "offline policy evaluation"
  - "longitudinal analysis"
  - "data governance"
  - "responsible AI"
